{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"AUDIT ANSWERED — it is TWO outliers, not one, and they pair up. Done while filing, so the ticket's audit criterion starts from evidence rather than a question.\n\nPER-FILE (declared): monitoring_1fa8.tf 1 alarm / actions yes. monitoring_88ab.tf 1 / yes. monitoring_autodeploy.tf 3 / yes (all three). monitoring_ws7.tf 1 / yes. monitoring.tf 4 alarms / 6 alarm_actions + 5 ok_actions. monitoring_s4b.tf 1 / NO. monitoring_s5.tf 1 / NO.\n\nLIVE (aws cloudwatch describe-alarms, count of AlarmActions per rebar-* alarm) — 12 alarms, exactly 2 with zero actions:\n    0  rebar-gerrit-voter-errors          (monitoring_s4b.tf)\n    0  rebar-gerrit-replication-errors    (monitoring_s5.tf)\n    1  rebar-autodeploy-errors\n    1  rebar-autodeploy-review-interrupts\n    1  rebar-gerrit-data-disk-high\n    1  rebar-gerrit-ec2-instance-check\n    1  rebar-gerrit-ec2-system-check\n    1  rebar-gerrit-g2p-dispatch-errors\n    1  rebar-gerrit-gate-down\n    1  rebar-gerrit-mirror-out-of-sync\n    1  rebar-review-bot-merge-change-errors\n    1  rebar-root-disk-pressure\nAll 12 currently read OK.\n\nREADING OF IT: the two silent alarms are the two story-S-numbered monitoring files, s4b and s5, which points at a single batch that omitted the actions rather than at a rule nobody follows — 10 of 12 wire it, so the convention exists and these two missed it. Per this ticket's own Approach note ('one outlier is a bug, four is a missing rule'), TWO sits at the boundary: my read is that it is still two bugs and does NOT justify inventing a checkable lint, because the omission is visibly against the prevailing pattern and a reviewer comparing to any neighbouring file would catch it. Worth revisiting only if a third appears.\n\nSCOPE CONSEQUENCE: this ticket should fix BOTH s4b and s5, not just voter_errors — the title names voter_errors because that is what the Bedrock cutover leans on, but replication_errors is the identical defect in the identical shape, and splitting them would mean two applies for one line each. Update the Scope when claiming."},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1785797137003779001,"uuid":"0dbc03a4-07d7-4731-b2ed-22f9c0bae96d"}